    <!--
        Where members land after signing out.

        The platform REQUIRES an absolute URL here ("The logout page URL must be
        an absolute URL."), which is why this is not the site-relative
        "/organisatorv1/login". The value is committed rather than generated by
        scripts/org-setup.mjs, because that path is unreachable here: its
        ensureLogoutUrl() first calls deriveSiteName(), which throws when a
        project holds more than one *.network-meta.xml, and this project holds
        two (frontend, Organisator). Committing it also means a plain
        "sf project deploy start" of this file re-applies the value instead of
        silently reverting it to the org default site login.

        Without this, /sfsites/s/logout redirects to the org's own login host at
        <host>.sandbox.my.salesforce.com/visualforce/session?url=... instead of
        to this app's /login. Passing retURL does not help: that endpoint has
        no return-URL parameter, the value only reappears echoed inside its own
        redirect. Measured 2026-10-02; see frontend/AGENTS.md.

        SANDBOX-SPECIFIC: the domain is hardcoded and must be changed for a
        different org.
    -->
    <logoutUrl>https://techandteach--devhub.sandbox.my.site.com/organisatorv1/login</logoutUrl>
